Human Interest is on a mission to ensure that people in all lines of work have access to retirement benefits. &nbsp;

More than half of all working Americans are not saving enough for their future. Too often, it’s because they are employed by a company that doesn’t offer a retirement plan. Human Interest is changing that by making it affordable and accessible for small and medium-sized businesses to offer employees a path to financial independence through retirement savings.

We’re a high-growth fintech company changing the retirement industry. We are backed by a number of investors. This includes funding from Marshall Wace and Baillie Gifford, as well as top investors such as BlackRock , TPG (The Rise Fund) , SoftBank, Glynn Capital , NewView Capital, USVP, Wing, Uncork, and more.

About the role

You will oversee a team of relationship managers and lead our engagement strategy across a portfolio of top-tier financial advisory firms. In this high-impact role, you will leverage your expertise in institutional relationship management to deepen partnerships, ensure strategic alignment, and drive new sales growth. Acting as a trusted executive partner to our corporate clients, you will guide a team dedicated to maximizing partnership value and elevating financial advisor engagement.&nbsp;

The ideal candidate is a driven strategic operator and relationship-builder who thrives in a matrixed organization, works seamlessly across functions, and is confident in navigating both internal leadership and senior external stakeholders. You will build relationships that translate into pipeline, revenue, and long-term market advantage.&nbsp;

This is an opportunity to play a pivotal role in how Human Interest partners at scale, particularly in the Financial Advisory channel, while shaping new ways to drive long-term value for our customers and our partners.

About the team

You will be responsible for working cross-functionally with leadership across Sales, Solutions, Marketing, Customer Success, and the Partnerships team to build the infrastructure that drives outcomes at scale. Your direct team will be focused on supporting sales, external partners relationships and net new partnerships.

What you get to do every day

• Team Leadership &amp; Development: Lead and mentor a high-performing team of Relationship Managers and Due Diligence process. Manage the cultivation, execution, and delivery of partner training and development for sales teams and stakeholders. Foster a culture of accountability, excellence, and partner-centricity.&nbsp;

• Build the infrastructure: Effectively enable advisor sales processes to work efficiently, create repeatable go-to-market motions, and build and manage an engaging events calendar.

• Identify &amp; execute on strategic initiatives: Work with partners on current initiatives and growth goals while driving near-term sales revenue.

• Partner Relationship Strategy: Own the strategic vision and relationship development for a portfolio of high-value Partnerships. Serve as the executive sponsor for key accounts, cultivating long-term, trusted relationships with senior leadership across RIAs, aggregators, asset managers, banks, and wealth managers.&nbsp;

• Turn relationships into outcomes: Create repeatable programs that generate pipeline, customers, and strategic value, not just logos or introductions.

• Raise the communication bar: Build exceptional presentations, pitches, and partner materials, and coach the team to do the same.

• Strategic Collaboration: Work cross-functionally with Product and Engineering leaders to define priorities, manage roadmaps, and execute the strategy for initiatives with new partner organizations. Collaborate with Sales, Finance, and Operations leadership to develop specific account management plans and partner support.&nbsp;

• Partner Enablement: Provide ongoing training, support, and resources to ensure partners are up-to-date with the latest product features, tools, and best

As a Commercial Strategy &amp; Program Manager in our Sales Strategy &amp; Operations team, you’ll manage the commercial go-to-market for on-top products across our international markets. With a particular focus on new product launches, you’ll build the business case, define the commercial approach and lead cross-functional execution from launch preparation through adoption and scaling. &nbsp;

You’ll be the central commercial point of contact for your assigned products, working closely with Product, Product Marketing, local sales leadership, Pricing, Finance and Analytics. You’ll turn analysis into decisions and strategy, align teams around measurable objectives and drive action when performance falls short.&nbsp; &nbsp;

This role is ideal for someone with a consulting or commercial strategy background who wants to combine analytical depth with hands-on responsibility for product commercialization. &nbsp;

What you’ll do: &nbsp;

• Own go-to-market plans: Define target customers, sales motions, market sequencing and launch priorities for on-top products. Drive execution against clear milestones and responsibilities. &nbsp;

